{"paper": "CHSL-Tier1-10-Jul-2024-Shift4.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "If the surface areas of two spheres are in the ratio of 49 : 81, then find the ratio of their volumes.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "For what value of k (k > 0) will the lines 5x + ky − 2 = 0 and (k + 1)x + 4y + 7 = 0 be parallel?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The details of books of 6 subjects on the first floor of the college library are given in the following table. The ratio of Maths and Computers to Circuit Theory and Graph Theory is:", "options": [{"text": "1 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "mixed-graphs", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "172", "added": false}, {"text": "127", "added": false}, {"text": "610", "added": false}, {"text": "106", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "729", "added": false}, {"text": "216", "added": false}, {"text": "343", "added": false}, {"text": "512", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "If the surface area of the sphere is 616 cm2, then the radius of the sphere is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "18.0cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14.0cm", "added": false}, {"text": "7.0cm", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 15% of the votes were invalid and one candidate got 52% of the total valid votes. If the total number of votes was 8000, what was the number of valid votes that the other candidate got?", "options": [{"text": "3264", "added": false}, {"text": "3536", "added": false}, {"text": "3840", "added": false}, {"text": "6800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "A number is divisible by 11 if and only if the difference of the sum of the digits in the even and odd positions in the number is:", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0 or multiple of 11", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "90°", "added": false}, {"text": "30°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Two numbers are respectively 61% and 35% less than a third number. The first number is what percentage of the second number?", "options": [{"text": "24%", "added": false}, {"text": "48%", "added": false}, {"text": "30%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Two chords AB and CD of a circle are produced to intersect each other at a point P outside the circle. If AB = 7 cm, BP = 4.2 cm and PD = 2.8 cm, then the length of CD is:", "options": [{"text": "11 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "18 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "16 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹4,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹12,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹15,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "If ‘÷’ means ‘×’, ‘×’ means ‘÷’, ‘+’ means ‘−’, ‘−’ means ‘+’, then 47 ÷ (10 × 5) + (4 − 5) − 6 is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "A and D", "added": false}, {"text": "B and E", "added": false}, {"text": "D and E", "added": false}, {"text": "A and E", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "Evaluate (9sin θ + 2 cos θ) / (9sin θ − 2cos θ), if 3 tan θ = 4.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "In an election between two candidates, Ananth and Aravind, Ananth got 55% of the total valid votes, and 20% of the votes were invalid. If the total number of votes was 30,000, find the number of valid votes that Aravind got.", "options": [{"text": "10800", "added": false}, {"text": "1080", "added": false}, {"text": "24000", "added": false}, {"text": "13200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "In an isosceles triangle, the vertex angle is four times the sum of the base angles. The measure of the square root of the vertex angle is:", "options": [{"text": "16°", "added": false}, {"text": "18°", "added": false}, {"text": "10°", "added": false}, {"text": "12°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A bucket contains a mixture of milk and water in the proportion of 7: 5. If 9 litres of milk is replaced by water, then the ratio becomes 7:9. How much milk was there in the bucket initially?", "options": [{"text": "36 litres", "added": false}, {"text": "35 litres", "added": false}, {"text": "30 litres", "added": false}, {"text": "25 litres", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "milk-water-and-alloys", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "∆ABC and ∆PQR are similar. The areas of these two triangles are 289 sq.cm and 576 sq.cm, respectively. If PR = 12 cm, then AC = ?", "options": [{"text": "7.25 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "8.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "12 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "6 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}]}